{"name":"Sweet Annie","hex":"#9c946e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet annie","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of sweet Annie."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet_annie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweet Annie","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sweet Annie\" is a song recorded by American country music group Zac Brown Band. It was released in August 2013 as the fourth single from the group's third major-label album, Uncaged. The song was written by Zac Brown, Wyatt Durrette, Sonia Leigh, and John Pierce. As of March 12, 2014 the single has sold 439,000 copies in the United States and has been certified Gold by the RIAA."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/SweetAnnie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_Annie"},{"title":"Artemisia annua","blocks":[{"text":"Artemisia annua, also known as sweet wormwood, sweet annie, sweet sagewort, annual mugwort or annual wormwood, is a common type of wormwood native to temperate Asia, but naturalized in many countries including scattered parts of North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Artemisia_annua.jpeg/330px-Artemisia_annua.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemisia_annua"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e1/SweetAnnie.jpg/250px-SweetAnnie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/SweetAnnie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e1/SweetAnnie.jpg/250px-SweetAnnie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASweetAnnie.jpg"},{"srcset":